/P 60 0 R
/E (Replacing raw collections with generic collections should be treated as an incremental modernization project, not a single large code change. The safest approach is to first inventory the codebase, enable compiler warnings, migrate simple collections, handle complex type relationships carefully, and then update public APIs using compatibility layers where necessary. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (A combination of compile-time checking, automated testing, regression testing, code review, backward compatibility, and risk management ensures that the migration improves type safety without disrupting existing functionality. Ultimately, generic collections provide stronger compile- time guarantees, reduce explicit casting, improve maintainability, and make the large codebase easier and safer to evolve. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
